## 4. Independent check of the five zero-reference claims

Method: `evidence/extent-check.mjs` enumerates every class member by its **4-space-indented
`function NAME(` start** (nested/inner functions are indented 8+, so they cannot be mistaken for a
member boundary) and runs each body from its start line to the line before the next member start.
No `awk` slicing, no guessed closing brace.

```
switchReturn:        extent 5570-5614 (45 lines), direct refs = 0
switchAssign:        extent 5508-5522 (15 lines), direct refs = 0
switchStatement:     extent 5492-5507 (16 lines), direct refs = 0
switchExpression:    extent 5523-5531 ( 9 lines), direct refs = 0
tryStatementLines:   extent 5187-5209 (23 lines), direct refs = 0
arrayBoundaryText:   extent 2566-2577, refs 2566 (self name), 2567 (the call)
lowerArrayBoundary:  extent 2578-2622, refs 2578 (def), 2580, 2607 (prepare), 2614 (render)
armLines:            extent 5615-5653, refs 5641, 5642 (isBoundary, arrayBoundaryText)
```

**All five zero-reference claims are CONFIRMED** for the literal bodies. The inference drawn from
them is what fails (section 3). Raw: `evidence/extent-check.txt`.

