## 5. The headline falsification: `lowerArrayBoundary` is not the single funnel

`SwiftArrayBoundary.prepare` / `.render` have **two production callers**, not one:

```
SwiftExpr.hx:2607, 2614   inside lowerArrayBoundary
SwiftDecl.hx:599,  604    static read-only array field initializer
```

`SwiftDecl.hx:581-606` builds its own `SwiftArrayPreparedOperand`, calls `prepare` and `render`
directly, and never touches `lowerArrayBoundary`. I verified this path is live and reachable:

```swift
public enum GapStatics {
    public static let values: ReadOnlyArray<Int32> = ReadOnlyArray(TiqianArray<Int32>([41]))   // line 106
}
public enum GapPaths {
    private static var slot: ReadOnlyArray<Int32> = ReadOnlyArray<Int32>()                      // line 122
}
```

Both are array crossings that convert correctly and **bypass `lowerArrayBoundary` entirely**.
The true single funnel is `SwiftArrayBoundary.prepare` + `render`; `lowerArrayBoundary` is one of
two producers feeding it. Raw: `evidence/prepare-render-callers.txt`.

