## 6. Side finding: the repo's own boundary fixture does not generate on this revision

`tests/swift-readonly-boundary/swift.hxml` fails:

```
swift target: array boundary has no prepared storage decision
```

This is `SwiftExpr.hx:2609` (`plan == null` after `prepare`). It reproduces with the two uncommitted
Swift-backend edits shadowed back to their `HEAD` content, so it is **not** caused by
`git diff` on `SwiftArrayBoundary.hx` / `SwiftDecl.hx`.

Method note (this matters, and I got it wrong once): Haxe `-cp` precedence is **last-wins**;
my first shadow attempt placed the shadow before `packages/compiler/reflaxe/swift` and was silently
ignored. I proved precedence with a marker that throws inside `prepare`
(`evidence/shadow-marker.log`, which also yields a clean call trace
`SwiftExpr.hx:746 → 2586 → 2642 → 2607`). The HEAD-shadow run with correct ordering is
`evidence/gen-readonly-head.log`.

Caveat: the worktree has other modifications (e.g. `samples/tests/NumberClassifyTests.hx`,
`package.json`) that I did not shadow, so I can only state that these two Swift-backend edits are
not the cause, not that HEAD is clean.

